  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "An interesting add-on for the upcoming Groups feature, I would like to see the ability for a Group to create a \"Team\" specifically for creation of worlds. Currently we can create a separate User which pretends it's a team, but that's still run by a single person and can have single person flaws.\nWhen using a Team, you can:\n- Create a Team which is simply a Group with special privileges\n- Add Teammates to a Team\n- Add Titles to Teammates\n- Ability to take over a Team if the Team Leader has gone AWOL for X days\n- Hook up metadata for Teammates like security settings (can you upload worlds on behalf of the team, etc)\n- Hook up metadata that can tie into the SDK, like GitHub information, Discord information, Discord Bots for API calls, etc.\nFrom a players perspective, not much has changed except for:\n- World author is now the team, and when you click on the world author it shows \"credits\" with the Teammates and their titles.\n- You can donate to the Team instead of individual users and it can be distributed equally or managed by the Team Leader. \nThis is just a very basic outline of the concept with my smol brain, please add suggestions here to help make this a big brain idea.",
